+  "problem": "## Observed\nThe frozen research contract (`badf-research`, #50 / WP-0031) has a **contract/schema asymmetry**. `skills/badf-research/SKILL.md` step 2 instructs the researcher to *\"resolve \u2026 stop conditions\"*, and the capability's purpose is bounded, governed uncertainty reduction \u2014 but `schemas/research-record.schema.json` carries `question`, `scope`, `known`, `unknown`, `hypotheses` and has **no first-class `stop_conditions`, `assumptions`, or `decision_context`**. The research scope contract is not machine-readable where it most matters: a run can be recorded with no declared bounded-termination, no separation of assumptions from evidence, and no named decision it serves.\n\n## Expected\nHarden the scope contract through this new governed WP (not by reopening #50), extend-only:\n- Add `stop_conditions` (bounded termination \u2014 the conditions under which the run stops), `assumptions` (kept distinct from claims/observations, per RSR-I03), and `decision_context` (the decision this research serves \u2014 reinforcing RESEARCH \u2260 DECISION while `authority.implementation_authority` stays `false`) as **first-class, required** research-record fields.\n- A new deterministic gate control: a material research run declares **non-empty `stop_conditions`** (no unbounded research scope), each assumption is a non-empty string distinct from evidence, and `decision_context.decision_question` is present. This becomes acceptance **control 19** \u2014 \"bounded research scope, machine-readable\".\n- These are **framing**, not evidence, so they stay OUT of the `evidence_digest` (which covers sources/claims/contradictions/experiments) \u2014 control 17 semantics unchanged.\n- Update the three shipped examples and align SKILL.md + acceptance.md. `badf-research` stays `DESIGNED`.\n\n## Evidence\n- `schemas/research-record.schema.json` properties missing: `stop_conditions, assumptions, decision_context`\n- `grep 'stop conditions' skills/badf-research/SKILL.md` \u2192 `stop conditions` (the skill promises what the schema cannot carry)\n\n## Unknowns\nNone for the scope contract. **Not in scope:** control 6 (source-digest freshness \u2014 needs a source fetch), the remaining 8 P0 subskills, and #77's \"canonical reference split\" (a docs refactor, deferrable). This WP closes only the scope-contract asymmetry.\n\n## Proposed work package\n`BADF-WP-0045`. Schema fields + control 19 in `validate_research_record`; the three examples updated; SKILL.md + acceptance.md aligned; `tests/test_badf_research.py` failing-first + mutation; own G07 self-dossier. C2. Brings research controls to 17/19 (control 6 freshness still open).\n\ndiscovered-by: operator review of the frozen contract (2026-08-29); overlaps external #69/#77 (left untouched) \u00b7 status: DISCOVERED\n\n",
